      "message": "\u003e Then, while handling the tablet mode notification the ASL accesses something that\u0027s not actually present/enabled and hits an error. Presumably that would be a bug and various protections should already be in place (#ifdefs, etc.)\n\nAll of this should be guarded already: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot/+/chromeos-2016.05:src/soc/amd/common/acpi/dptc.asl;l\u003d20\n\n\u003e Or maybe that\u0027s too paranoid of a thought. Also, beyond landing the CL and seeing if things blow up, I\u0027m not sure how to validate the CL otherwise.\n\nYeah, building with the whole stack is the only real way to test all of this.",
